  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday Night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1037 AM CDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\nAs Tuesday rolls around, we'll start to see the effects of \nstrengthening upper level ridging across the mid-Mississippi and \nOhio valleys. Temperatures will start to climb a few degrees above \nnormal and will likely stay there for several days. No record \nbreaking heat, but mid to upper 70s will be common in the afternoon \nalong with cool mornings mainly in the 40s. The other thing that \nwill be common is the lack of rain. 240 hours in the GFS and Euro \nand no rain in sight. This means worsening drought conditions when \nwe're already hurting. Light winds throughout the forecast should \nmitigate any real fire weather concerns, but you may want to start \nthinking twice before initiating any outdoor fires for a while. \nMaybe November will bring much needed rain.",
